[transport.ts:110](E:/projects/virtual-office/src/lib/meeting-notes/ai/adapters/transport.ts:110)  
  A provider or gatewayâ€™s 307/308 causes `fetch` to resend the POST internally, bypassing the one-fetch guard. 
Actual SDK probes produced two POSTs followed by `preprocessing_rejected`; redirecting to a refused connection 
produced `never_sent` after the first endpoint received the request. A cross-origin redirect also forwarded 
Anthropicâ€™s API-key header. **Fix:** force `redirect: 'manual'`, classify the original response, and test redirect 
chains and credential forwarding.

- **C-2 â€” Medium â€” Timeout and cancellation can return successful drafts.** 
[adapters/index.ts:125](E:/projects/virtual-office/src/lib/meeting-notes/ai/adapters/index.ts:125)  
  Abort handling runs only when `finish === 'incomplete'`. If the provider emits valid draft text and a stop marker, 
then the connection stalls before completion, the SDK silently ends on abort and the adapter returns success. Probes 
returned `ok:true` after both a 300-ms timeout and a caller abort. **Fix:** check `control.reason` after iteration 
regardless of finish state; return a counted timeout/cancellation and discard the draft.

- **C-3 â€” Medium â€” Multipart creation lacks origin protection.** 
[transcript/route.ts:27](E:/projects/virtual-office/src/app/api/meeting-notes/transcript/route.ts:27)  
