spec-interview/phase-6-meeting-notes/TRACK.md:479:- `POST /api/meeting-notes/[id]/ai/process` {ticket, 
idempotencyKey?}: origin guard + auth → rate limit `meeting-note:ai-process` 20/60 s → ticket signature/expiry → 
binding (user ≠ 409, company ≠ 404, note/key mismatch 409) → service-role admission (actor = dbUser.id) → normalize → 
preflight → mark dispatched → adapter (request.signal + timeout, default 180 s, optional 
`MEETING_NOTES_AI_TIMEOUT_MS`) → membership/editor/note recheck → settle. 200 {operationId, status, replay, 
sourceRevision, transcriptId, draft|null, usage|null}; replay = status only. Errors: 400 TICKET_INVALID, 410 
TICKET_EXPIRED, 409 BINDING_MISMATCH / NOT_CONFIGURED / SETTINGS_STALE {settings} / SOURCE_STALE / OPERATION_ENDED / 
DRAFT_DISCARDED, 429 LIMIT_REACHED {limit, used, usageDay, resetAt}, 404/403 (also when access lost while processing → 
discarded), 422 TRANSCRIPT_TOO_LONG_FOR_MODEL (released), 502 adapter failure, 499 CANCELLED, 503 UNAVAILABLE. Never 
the key, transcript, or provider text.
spec-interview/phase-6-meeting-notes/TRACK.md:480:- Settlement: preflight refusal / client gone before mark → 
released; success with client present + rights + note → succeeded; success but client left or access lost → discarded; 
processed_failure → failed (discarded if client left); preprocessing_rejected → refunded; never_sent after mark → 
refunded; unexpected error before mark → released (refunded if mark committed); after mark → failed; settle 
changed=false/other status → draft dropped.
